{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":88,"name":"Fransina Stradling","username":"f.stradling","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.igelsociety.org/f.stradling/{size}/9_2.png","created_at":"2022-01-13T14:00:32.927Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAston Stylistics Research Group\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cstrong\u003eApplied Stylistics: Symposium on Friday 6th May 2022\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollowing the success of our 2021 symposium, we are delighted to\u003cbr\u003e\ninvite proposals for a one day hybrid event on Friday 6th May 2022.\u003cbr\u003e\nWe are looking for proposals for twenty minute papers from\u003cbr\u003e\nresearchers whose work comes under the broad umbrella of ‘applied\u003cbr\u003e\nstylistics’.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are taking ‘applied’ to cover a wide range of work that\u003cbr\u003e\ninvestigates any external-facing issue through the use of stylistic\u003cbr\u003e\nmethods and approaches and thus may examine different kinds of\u003cbr\u003e\ntexts and datasets. Papers might explore areas that include, but are not\u003cbr\u003e\nlimited to\u003cbr\u003e\n• literary and language education\u003cbr\u003e\n• professional and creative writing\u003cbr\u003e\n• reading and culture\u003cbr\u003e\n• stylistics and law\u003cbr\u003e\n• stylistics and health communication\u003cbr\u003e\n• stylistics and politics\u003cbr\u003e\n• stylistics and translation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are particularly keen to receive proposals from ECRs and doctoral\u003cbr\u003e\nresearchers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbstracts (maximum of 200 words, excluding references) should be\u003cbr\u003e\nsubmitted to \u003cspan class=\"email-redacted\"\u003e[email redacted]\u003c/span\u003e and \u003cspan class=\"email-redacted\"\u003e[email redacted]\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nby Monday 7th February 2022. Please indicate if you submitting a\u003cbr\u003e\nproposal for a paper to be delivered in person or online.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMarcello Giovanelli and Chloe Harrison\u003cbr\u003e\nCo-Directors, Aston Stylistics Research Group\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://appliedstylistics.wordpress.com/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://s1.wp.com/i/favicon.ico\" class=\"site-icon\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://appliedstylistics.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eappliedstylistics.wordpress.com\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:440/330;\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://appliedstylistics.files.wordpress.com/2020/10/ugo-mendes-donelli-e4fbcdbyhji-unsplash.jpg?fit=440%2C330\" class=\"thumbnail\" width=\"440\" height=\"330\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://appliedstylistics.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003e(no title)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eVisit the post for more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"updated_at":"2022-01-13T14:00:56.733Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":23,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":161.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":79,"topic_slug":"cfp-for-applied-stylistics-symposium","display_username":"Fransina Stradling","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://appliedstylistics.wordpress.com/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":fa